Ground-truth capture trigger for the pinned PCSX2 reference build.

Why this patch exists
---------------------
Capturing a hardware reference for a scene deep in attract needs the dump to
start at a *guest-semantic* moment, not at a wall-clock offset and not when a
human decides the picture looks right. PCSX2 can only start a GS dump from a
hotkey, so every reference this project owns was staged by hand: not
reproducible, impossible to re-run when a checkpoint moves, and it caps the
oracle at the handful of scenes somebody sat through. (Injecting the hotkey
from the outside is not an option either — this host denies osascript the
accessibility permission that sending keystrokes needs.)

This adds a host-side controller that watches an EE word each vsync and starts
a bounded, deterministically-named GS dump when the guest enters a requested
(phase, script, step) coordinate. It is purely observational:

  * it never writes guest memory, never changes timing, never changes GS state;
  * it starts the dump through exactly the call the GSDumpMultiFrame hotkey
    makes (`GSQueueSnapshot`), on the same thread, with the same arguments;
  * with `RRV_GT_CAPTURE` unset it reads one getenv and does nothing.

The reference-purity claim is not "the patch looks harmless". Every capture
logs the ELF probe word 0x2206F8 beside the dump it triggered, and
scripts/gt_capture.py re-captures A1 and A3 and diffs them against the trusted
2026-08-02 references before any new checkpoint is used (docs/TESTING.md
T-GT-AUTO).

Applies to PCSX2 d5f75c9e42064a77036466f1f4594b0507888633.
Build with scripts/build_pcsx2_gt_capture.sh, which clones the pinned revision
into a scratch tree and never touches the user's working tree.

